From decdab0ca3ec79a2821370a9b074312a1d3be5e5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 12:41:09 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Guest networks: DNS redirect kept, VPN server clients, mDNS
 plan, passcode (102.8 line)

- rc/reaper_guest.c: the guests' DNS redirect is put back after the nat table is restored (a
  portal start and the WAN monitor replace the whole table, and signed-in portal guests then
  reached any resolver).
- rc/reaper_guest.c: clients of the router's own WireGuard / OpenVPN server may open connections
  into an isolated guest network again, as before v3.7.7: such a connection goes on to the stock
  server chains, which decide by the server's own access setting, and the network may answer it. A
  guest still cannot open a connection to a VPN client. Not into a Guest Portal network, not while
  the network's kill switch is on. Field report, GT-BE98.
- rc/reaper_guest.c, rc/services.c: which networks mDNS serves. avahi no longer answers on a
  network guest isolation closes; the reflector joins the main network and every network with
  Access Intranet on, never a Guest Portal and never a network with Set AP Isolated on, and avahi
  is restarted only when that plan changes.
- rc/services.c: the Free Wi-Fi passcode is honoured again at portal start (it had been forced off
  on 2026-11-12); a guest-network change starts the VPN client the network is bound to.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
